    "8b_10b_encoding_note": "The PCI Express Physical Layer uses the IBM 8b/10b code published by Widmer + Franaszek in IBM J. Res. Dev. Vol 27 #5 (Sept 1983) — same code as Fibre Channel, Gigabit Ethernet 1000BASE-X, Serial ATA, and InfiniBand 1x. Provides DC balance + ≤ 5-bit run length + 12 unique 'comma' K-codes used by PCI Express as Special Symbols.",
